      "humanEdibility": ["s1:p6", "s1:p7"]
    }
  },
  {
    "taxonId": 1229224,
    "summary": "A perennial groundcover found in southern Africa, lobster bush has hairy, succulent grey-green leaves with a strong scent likened to cannabis or skunk. Purple-blue flower spikes appear twice yearly, in late summer and late winter. Fresh leaves are steeped to make a mint-like tea.",
    "humanEdibility": "yes",
    "edibilityNote": "Fresh leaves are steeped to make a tea described as similar to mint tea.",
